It builds on, but does not redistribute, the following software:

- DeepInfer (https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepInfer), Copyright DeepSeek, Apache License 2.0.
  The Docker image clones it at a pinned commit. patches/deepinfer-sequence-block-table.patch is a
  modification of one DeepInfer source file and is distributed under the same license. The drop-in
  packages in sm120/ reimplement the Python APIs of DeepSeek's FlashMLA, DeepGEMM, DeepEP and
  DeepSelect libraries as DeepInfer calls them.

- b12x (https://pypi.org/project/b12x/), Apache License 2.0, installed from PyPI. Its upstream
  issue tracker is part of FlashInfer (https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer).
  patches/b12x-tiny-decode-swiglu.patch is a modification of b12x and is distributed under the
  same license.

- DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash model weights and their reference inference code are NOT included. They are
  available from DeepSeek under their own license terms. The validation tools in tools/ref/ expect
  the user to supply them.

- Some approaches were taken over, as ideas and reimplemented here, from studying vLLM
  (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm, Apache License 2.0) and community forks of it that serve
  DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash on RTX PRO 6000: keeping the engram tables in pinned host memory gathered by the
  GPU, and the evaluation scenarios. No vLLM source code is included.
